Z||000000||85ZainoGT||12-29-2001||09:14 PM||||ok this is a serious question, would a Ford Escape beat my car? 87gt auto? lol... im jw, cause I rode in one las night and it wasnt slow... 3.6l dual overhead cams or somethin like that?<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW3bsmall2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||BlackStang95||12-30-2001||02:30 AM||||As the resident ford guy, the tests I've seen on the escape put them in the high 8 second 0-60 range and mid 16's in the 1/4.  Hell of a performer for an entry level suv.  I think it would be close and if your gt is getting up on mileage it might put the escape over the top.  The explorer, surprisingly, is an even better performer...hitting up the upper 7 second 0-60 range.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||firstfiero||12-30-2001||11:17 AM||||     My sportrac is actually pretty quick for an suv. I test drove an escape and their not bad in the power area at all.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||12-30-2001||11:32 AM||||It would be close... Escapes do run in the upper 8's to 60.  I know my 88 Formula auto runs an 8.7 to 60.  My engine isn't in great shape either... 84K miles and it shows with some oil burning, bad valve seals and who knows what else.  In its day it may have been a bit faster.  However, the escape would give it a run.  The escape uses a 3.0L DOHC engine... I believe 200 HP.  Its good performance for an economy SUV.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||12-30-2001||02:24 PM||||Speaking of Escapes...that is the rental car we have here. I'm not so fond of it, it feels cheap. It also feels fairly slow 0-60 but has decent pickup when trying to pass someone.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">                 <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa1/showdates.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Events 2002</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tarheel Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hybrid2M6||12-30-2001||03:28 PM||||I drive them all the time since I work at a Ford dealership. I dont think the auto version would be able to beat you, but possibly the 5spd version with an ok driver behind the wheel. I'm also not too impressed with them either.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/customgfx.jpg"> <BR>1986 SE IronDuke<BR>Adjustable Touring Wing<BR>American Racing Carrera's<BR> -225/50VR16 Falken Ziex 502<BR> -225/45ZR17 Falken Azenis<BR>Cleared and Painted(red) Tail lights||||reg||13
Z||000006||Fformula88||12-30-2001||09:54 PM||||I have a side note on their "cheapness".  Ford has used their CD4E auto tranny in the V6's.  Its a fairly new automatic that first appeared in 1994 and has found its way into a few cars, notably the Contour/Mystique, Cougar, Probe (4 cyl only) and Escape/Tribute.  These are some of the worst transmissions on the planet for reliability.  Despite numerous running changes to them, they still fail at an extraordinarily high rate.  I definately wouldn't recommend owning one of these things past its warrenty!||||reg||1
Z||000007||falconhulk||12-31-2001||12:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hybrid2M6:<BR><B>I drive them all the time since I work at a Ford dealership. I dont think the auto version would be able to beat you, but possibly the 5spd version with an ok driver behind the wheel. I'm also not too impressed with them either.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your post confused me becasue i was sure that the V6 200hp engine was only available with the auto trans.  I checked and thats correct.  The 5 speed manual is available with the crappy 4cy.  So I think the auto is the only thing that has a chance!!  Since you work for a ford dealer you should have known that.  FYI <A HREF="http://www6.forddirect.fordvehicles.com/Dispatch.jsp?__action=&__action2=&.CurrentState=ZipCode&processZipCodeAndModel=true&selectModel=Escape&processZipCode=25425" TARGET=_blank>http://www6.forddirect.fordvehicles.com/Dispatch.jsp?__action=&__action2=&.CurrentState=ZipCode&processZipCodeAndModel=true&selectModel=Escape&processZipCode=25425</A> <P>||||reg||1
